This document describes how to interact with the API endpoints of my capstone project, covering user roles, job posts, and applications.

USERS API

Employer Profile

Endpoint: `/api/users/EmployerProfile/`

Methods supported:

- GET: List all employer profiles.
- POST: Create a new employer profile.
- GET `/id/`: Get employer profile by ID.
- PUT `/id/`: Update employer profile.
- DELETE `/id/`: Delete employer profile.

Fields returned:

- `user`: User ID
- `company`: Company name
- `industry`: Industry
- `is_hiring`: Boolean

Example response in json format:
{
  "id": 1,
  "user": 3,
  "company": "InnovateTech Inc.",
  "industry": "Information Technology",
  "is_hiring": true
}

Worker Profile

Endpoint: `/api/users/Worker_profile/`

Methods supported:

- GET: List all worker profiles.
- POST: Create a new worker profile.
- GET `/id/`: Get worker profile by ID.
- PUT `/id/`: Update worker profile.
- DELETE `/id/`: Delete worker profile.

Fields that will be returned:

- `user`: User ID
- `skills`: Worker’s skill set
- `experience`: Description of past experience
- `portfolio`: Optional portfolio URL

Example response in json format:
{
  "id": 2,
  "user": 5,
  "skills": "Python, Django, REST APIs",
  "experience": "Over 2 years of backend development experience",
  "portfolio": "https://github.com/johndoe"
}


JOBPOST API

Endpoint: `/api/jobs/jobs/`

Supported methods:

- GET: Retrieve all job posts
- POST: Create new job (auto-assigns employer)
- GET `/id/`: Get specific job
- PUT `/id/`: Update job
- DELETE `/id/`: Delete job

Job post includes:

- `title`
- `description`
- `created_at`
- `employer`

Example in json format:
{
  "id": 12,
  "title": "Senior Backend Developer",
  "description": "We are hiring a senior Django developer with at least 3 years of experience.",
  "created_at": "2025-04-09T09:15:23Z",
  "employer": 1
}

APPLICATION API

Applying to a Job

POST `/api/applications/Apply/{job_id}/`

- Auto-fills `job` and `applicant`
- Blocks duplicate applications

Example response in json format:
{
  "id": 5,
  "job": 12,
  "applicant": 4,
  "applied_since": "2025-04-09T10:01:03Z",
  "status": "pending"
}

Updating Application Status

Employers only.

Endpoints:

- GET `/api/applications/update/`: List applications
- GET `/id/`: View application
- PUT `/id/`: Update status

Accepted status: `pending`, `accepted`, `rejected`

PUT request example:

{
  "status": "accepted"
}
```

Response in json format:


{
  "id": 5,
  "job": 12,
  "applicant": 4,
  "applied_since": "2025-04-09T10:01:03Z",
  "status": "accepted"
}


SETTINGS

- Custom user model: `users.CustomUser`
- Auth: TokenAuthentication
- Important apps: DRF, drf_yasg, corsheaders

---

NOTES

- Auth is required
- Employer is auto-set on job creation
- One application per job per user
- Employers only modify their own applications
- Validation ensures clean inputs
